      </characteristics>
      <comment>Black Coach</comment>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Zombie Pirate" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="9c91-c09d-e8c4-b393" page="D&apos;Ruiz&apos;s Vampire Coast for Warhammer The Old World">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="cd3b-a5a4-e185-5a9d">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="b007-7d58-4f14-1e01">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="59f9-ccf5-1155-fb05">0</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5b6b-1427-2a45-dd0c">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ab43-8b61-83e7-d090">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">4</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Throwing Bombs" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="6c69-2099-d730-b0d2">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">If unengaged, a unit with this rule that is charged in its front arc inflicts D3 automatic hits on the charger, resolved at Strength 3, Armour Penetration -1, plus an additional D3 hits per point of rank bonus (max +3).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Crew" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="f518-70e5-57ba-de92">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During the Command subphase of your turn, the Character can attempt to inspire their allies by making a Leadership test using their own Leadership. If successful, choose one unit with the Crew special rule within 12&quot; and grant it one of the following benefits until the start of your next turn (does not affect characters joined to the unit):
- The unit improves its Wet Powder (X) skill by +1.
- The unit gains the special rule Reserve Move.
- The unit improves its Weapon Skill by +1 (does not affect mounts).
For example, a unit with Wet Powder (6+) will have it upgraded to Wet Powder (5+)</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Wet Powder" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="d358-920a-d368-7363">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Models with Ballistic Skill 0 that carry ranged weapons will always hit with the result in parentheses in this rule and will not suffer any penalties that do not come from a magical source (such as a spell or enemy ability).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
      <comment>The pirates of the Vampire Coast carry a lot of gunpowder, from pistols to large cannons. Despite they are not skilled, they still retain some of their former aim, now emphasized by the spells cast by Harkon.</comment>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Aquatic (Vampire Coast)" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="fe36-b51c-b523-8520">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">Models with this special rule do not suffer any modifiers to their Movement characteristic when moving through any difficult or dangerous terrain feature which has been designated a ‘water feature’. This might include shallow streams or fords, swampy ground, fast flowing rivers, ponds or lakes, and players should agree prior to the game if any terrain is a water feature.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Pirate Blunderbluss" typeId="a378-c633-912d-11ce" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="eaa8-e08d-73d2-8216">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="R" typeId="2360-c777-5e07-ed58">12&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="ac19-f99c-72e9-a1a7">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="9429-ffe7-2ce5-e9a5">-1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="5f83-3633-336b-93b4">Multiple Shots (D3), Volley Fire</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="772a-a7ff-f6b3-df71">Note: A model armed with a Hailshot blunderbuss suffers no negative modifiers for firing at long range, for using the Multiple Shots (D3) special rule, or whilst making a Stand &amp; Shoot charge reaction.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Deck Gunner" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="ac3c-21a9-5da3-37d6">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="cd3b-a5a4-e185-5a9d">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="b007-7d58-4f14-1e01">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="59f9-ccf5-1155-fb05">0</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5b6b-1427-2a45-dd0c">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ab43-8b61-83e7-d090">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">4</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Falconets" typeId="a378-c633-912d-11ce" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="b166-bc43-2898-d776">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="R" typeId="2360-c777-5e07-ed58">36&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="ac19-f99c-72e9-a1a7">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="9429-ffe7-2ce5-e9a5">-1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="5f83-3633-336b-93b4">Armor Bane (2), Move or Shoot</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="772a-a7ff-f6b3-df71"/>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Bloated Corpse" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="4962-7b8e-f33b-b170">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="cd3b-a5a4-e185-5a9d">2D6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="b007-7d58-4f14-1e01">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="59f9-ccf5-1155-fb05">0</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5b6b-1427-2a45-dd0c">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ab43-8b61-83e7-d090">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">4</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Gas Explosion" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="e1f6-38d9-4fdb-b2e6">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">When the Bloated Corpse is eliminated, any enemy or friendly model within 6&quot; of it will suffer one Strength 2 hit that do not allow an Armor Save (Ward Saves can be used normally).


Units in contact with a eliminated Bloated Corpse rolls only a single D6 when making a &apos;Overrun&apos; roll (rather than the usual 2D6).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Depth Guard" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="8c30-23e6-b7a0-faaf">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="cd3b-a5a4-e185-5a9d">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="b007-7d58-4f14-1e01">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="59f9-ccf5-1155-fb05">3</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5b6b-1427-2a45-dd0c">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ab43-8b61-83e7-d090">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">1</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">7</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Cursed Weapons" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="0875-b296-0fab-9a30">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A hand weapon carried by a model with this special rule has the Magic Attacks special rule and an Armor Piercing attribute of -1.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Luthor Harkon" typeId="b070-143a-73f-2772" typeName="Model" hidden="false" id="6a79-2f7c-3333-af59">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="M" typeId="cd3b-a5a4-e185-5a9d">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="WS" typeId="b007-7d58-4f14-1e01">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="BS" typeId="59f9-ccf5-1155-fb05">7</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="5b6b-1427-2a45-dd0c">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="T" typeId="ab43-8b61-83e7-d090">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="W" typeId="83ed-7b82-bf1f-e558">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="I" typeId="73b1-abe5-72f8-41e2">6</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="A" typeId="dddc-9fbd-b0fd-a480">4</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="c435-6b14-f77e-3c72">9</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Lore of the Deep" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="316f-a990-f940-70fb">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A Wizard with the ‘Lore of the Deep’ special rule may discard one of their randomly generated spells as normal. When they do so, they may select instead either the signature spell of their chosen Lore of Magic, or one of the spells listed below:

• Fog of the Damned
• Spiteful Shot
• Kraken Pulls</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Multiple Personality" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="4aa0-d1d7-e658-4654">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">At the start of each Vampire Coast player’s turn, roll 1D6 and consult the following table.
The effects last until the start of the player’s next turn and only affect Luthor Harkon:


1) Mental Block: He suffers a -1L penalty and the special rule Stupidity and he must check for it inmediatly.


2) Ruthless: His ranged weapon gains the special rules Multiple Shots (1D3) and Move and Shoot. He can reroll any rolls To Hit of natural 1.


3) Narcissist: He gains the special rule Hold Your Ground (see page 7).


4) Deranged: He gains the special rules Frenzy. Also he can repeat the failing wound rolls in close combat or with the weapon DitchDisputes. Each time he makes a wound roll 1d6, with 6+ he recovers a lost wound.


5) Mastery: He gains a +1 modifier to his Cast and Dispel Spells rolls.


6) Clear Mind: Applies all the effects from results 2 through 5.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Slann Relics" typeId="d29c-a3fb-dcdf-29d6" typeName="Enchanted Items" hidden="false" id="1648-3683-fb6b-ce00">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="cea7-7573-475d-cc1d">Luthor Harkon has the special rules Magic Resistance (2) and Ward Save (5+). 


Additionally, if he suffers a miscast, he must roll twice and choose the lower result.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Ditch Disputes" typeId="a378-c633-912d-11ce" typeName="Weapon" hidden="false" id="92b2-4b9e-e9c4-c3f3">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="R" typeId="2360-c777-5e07-ed58">18&quot;</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="S" typeId="ac19-f99c-72e9-a1a7">5</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="AP" typeId="9429-ffe7-2ce5-e9a5">-2</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Special Rules" typeId="5f83-3633-336b-93b4">Magical Attacks, Multiple Wounds (D3), Quick Shot</characteristic>
        <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="772a-a7ff-f6b3-df71">In close combat, this miniature can make an additional attack with this weapon&apos;s profile</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Command Orders" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="8078-a46c-2f17-0727">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During the Command subphase of your turn, the Character can attempt to inspire their allies by making a Leadership test using their own Leadership. If successful, choose one unit with the Crew special rule within 12&quot; and grant it, their mounts and any character joined one of the following benefits until the start of your next turn:
- The unit improves its Wet Powder (X) skill by +1.
- The unit gains the special rule Reserve Move.
- The unit improves its Weapon Skill by +1.
 For example, a unit with Wet Powder (6+) will have it upgraded to Wet Powder (5+).</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Fleet Banner" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="843f-471a-e83c-21b4">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">A Fleet Captain who has been made your Battle Standard Bearer replaces the &quot;Hold Your Position&quot; Rule given in the Warhammer: the Old World rulebook with the version given below:
“Hold Your Ground”: Friendly units within the Battne Standard Bearer’s Command range may re-roll any fained Leadership test. In addition, friendly units within the Battle Standard Bearer’s Command range reduce the number of Wounds lost due to the Unstamne special rule by D3.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Curse of the Risen One" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="33a9-e003-e70e-48ad">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">This Vampire has a +1 modifier to its Wounds attribute</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Marine Vigor" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="5dc1-20c8-4d9c-9a3a">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">The character can re-roll failed Regeneration rolls</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Fleet Commander" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="4674-e819-5e4b-39ca">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">The character can use their special rule Command Order twice</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Master of Black Magic" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="583d-c5e6-a157-6368">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">This Vampiric Power can only be acquired by a Fleet Admiral who is a Level 2 Wizard, or by a Vampire Captain who is a Level 1 Wizard. 


This vampire increases his Level of Wizardry Level by 1.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Supernatural Vision" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="fda3-51ac-03f1-9e97">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">This Vampire gains a +1 modifier to his Ballistic Skill attribute and can fire his non-magical ranged weapon twice.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Sea Madness" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="0a9c-504f-b5b3-9b30">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">At the start of each Vampire Coast player&apos;s turn, roll 1D6 and consult the following table, the effect last until the start of your next turn:


1) Madness: The vampire lashes out against his comrades with rage in his eyes and foam at his mouth. 
The unit the vampire is in, or the vampire himself if not in a unit, suffers 2d3 Strength 5 hits with AP-.


2) Frenzy: Enraged, the vampire rushes into battle.
The vampire gains the special rule Frenzy.


3) Bloody: The vampire seeks only pain in his enemies. 
The vampire can re-roll wound rolls of 1.


4) Mastery: Majestic, the creature radiates nobility. 
The vampire gains +1 Weapon Skill, Ballistic Skill, and Leadership.


5) Supernatural Speed: Reflexes impossible to follow. 
The vampire gains +1 Attack, Initiative, and the special rule Quick Shot.


6) Martial Egocentrism: In his mind, he sees himself asan unbeatable and immortal being. 
The vampire gains +1 Strength, must issue and accept challenges, and can re-roll hit rolls of 1.


Note: Only the vampire gain these effects, not the mount he is on.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
    <profile name="Lord of the Sea" typeId="c1ac-c1c8-f9d5-9673" typeName="Special Rule" hidden="false" id="495b-cd56-1a5e-27d9">
      <characteristics>
        <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9f84-4221-785a-db50">During the Command subphase of your turn, this Vampire can attempt to resurrect creatures fallen from the night by making a Leadership check (using its own Leadership). 


If this check is passed, a single friendly unit of Deck Droppers, Bat Swarms, or Scurvy Dogs that are within 12&quot; of this model regain D6 lost wounds.</characteristic>
      </characteristics>
    </profile>
